{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-18T14:58:31.076Z","data":{"text":"Task 3 is complete. Summary:\n\n**What I did**\n- Copied the five TypeScript-printed goldens byte-for-byte into `crates/kernel/specs/tests/golden/` (verified with `cmp`) and the three frozen living specs into `tests/fixtures/living/`, each with `spec.md` and `osq.yml`.\n- Wrote `tests/golden_support/mod.rs` (with `digest.rs`, `entries.rs`, `diff.rs`): the FNV-1a 64 digest rule (strings > 64 UTF-16 units hashed, `path`/`capability` and object keys as written), builders for all five golden entries, and `first_difference` naming the RFC 6901 pointer of the first disagreement.\n- Wrote `tests/golden_cases.rs` (proves *Living fixtures match TypeScript* plus fast digest/pointer cases) and `tests/golden_corpus.rs` (two ignored corpus tests, backed by `golden_corpus/{corpus,archive,living,scan}.rs`, proving *Archived documents match TypeScript* over folders 001–214 by path with set equality, and *Living specs read*).\n- No `src/` line needed fixing: every parse already equals its golden entry, so the fast-case/fixture branch of acceptance didn't apply.\n\n**Verification**\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-specs --test golden_cases --test golden_corpus -- --include-ignored` → green.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` → green.\n- `cargo mutants -p osq-kernel-specs` → 323 caught, 35 unviable, 0 missed; a test-file-only diff yields \"No mutants to filter\", so the verify's diff step adds no new mutant. Removed the `mutants.out` my manual run created.\n\n**One deviation** (in the result file): the helper is included as `pub mod golden_support;`, not `mod golden_support;`, so each test binary doesn't flag the other's entry builders as dead code under `-D warnings`.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/215-rust-specs-parse/.run/results/3.md`."}}
